{#
  What this build was rendered from, for the publish gate to check against.

  scripts/check-build.mjs asserts things about the board that only mean
  something if the data it reads is the data the pages were rendered from. It
  used to read the committed fallbacks directly, which is right for its own
  hermetic build and wrong for the deploy, where the pages come from a live
  fetch: every content check then gated a board that was not the one shipping.

  Emitted as a build artefact rather than a published endpoint. It is not
  linked, carries nothing /data/latest.json does not already say in a
  supported shape, and is not part of the data contract - the schema-versioned
  endpoints are.
